; Split-horizon zone for mail.peetvandesande.com.
;
; This name exists publicly as a CNAME to an OVH VPS (ruby,
; vps-5ca50660.vps.ovh.net, 145.239.73.18). Ruby only serves mail on its
; WireGuard address: 993 answers on 192.168.254.254 and times out on the
; public address, so a client that resolves the public name simply hangs.
;
; Both of ruby's dummy0 addresses are reachable from the LAN over wgclient1:
; 192.168.254.254 via dst_net4399 and the router's 19000 rules, and
; fd33:5692:1834:254::254 via the 19000 rules and table 1001's route6 entries -
; see router/README.md. Nothing here routes; this only names them.
;
; The AAAA was left out until 2026-10-16, because the v6 address did not answer
; from the LAN before the 19000 rules went in on 2026-10-11. Checked from ruby,
; sourced from 254::254: the router's LAN ULA answers ping and HTTP. Both
; addresses offer the same mail services - 993, 4190 and 25 - and neither has
; submission (465/587), which ruby binds only on its wg0 addresses.
;
; The zone is deliberately the SINGLE NAME, not peetvandesande.com - a zone for
; the parent would shadow www and everything else in the domain with an empty
; internal zone. peetvandesande.com is DNSSEC-signed, so this override needs a
; matching addNTA() on Delphi or every lookup here SERVFAILs.
;
; GENERATED by dns/ansible - do not edit this file by hand.
; The source is dns/ansible/group_vars/all.yml. Change it there and run
;   cd dns/ansible && ansible-playbook zones.yml
; which rewrites this file, bumps the serial only if the contents changed,
; pushes it to Pythia and reloads just this zone.
$TTL 3600
$ORIGIN mail.peetvandesande.com.

@       IN  SOA pythia.home. hostmaster.home. (
                2026102105  ; serial
                3600        ; refresh
                900         ; retry
                604800      ; expire
                3600 )      ; negative TTL

@       IN  NS      pythia.home.

@       IN  A       192.168.254.254          ; ruby, over wgclient1
@       IN  AAAA    fd33:5692:1834:254::254  ; ruby's dummy0, over wgclient1
